 "note": "XS, 13 platforms. R-01's strait upside down and with three ferries of their own: each crossing is a 1-bridge ferry swinging out and back on its own clock, the top and bottom ones in step, the middle one half a cycle off (one crossing is always about to open). The dry way is the bottom stone, whose owner retracts the outer roads into it. Curved belt roads from each home to the middle bank. Finale: the banks.",
 "geometricSymmetry": true,
 "experimental": false,
 "ruleWaivers": {
  "L05": "the finale's decision is the ferry between the banks (a hazard on its own clock: when to send, which lane); the rulebook's stand-in reads a hazard ferry as a fixed deck, so L05 cannot see it (round R, 2026-11-05)"
 },
